.\" Manpage for obfuscate
.TH OBFUSCATE 1 "November 2025" "1.0" "Obfuscate Manual"
.SH NAME
obfuscate \- create a Swift file you can use in an app that obfuscates the input. Typically, the input is an API secret key.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obfuscate
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBobfuscate\fR is a command-line utility to create a Swift file you can use in an app that obfuscates the input.
Typically, the input is an API secret key.

The command will print the output to the console or, optionally, to a file in the cwd

You then have a file that produces a `Secrets` enum, which allows you to retrieve the original API key without having the key anywhere in your source control system. It is also not directly within the `Secrets` file.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Display version information.
.TP
.B -c, --check
Flag to run a check that the output file will decode the input correctly
.TP
.B -f, --fileName
You can optionally write the output to a file, so you can import it into your app
.TP
.B -k, --key \fIname\fR=\fIsecret\fR
A secret, and the name of the \fBSecrets\fR property that returns it. The name is everything before the first \fB=\fR, so the secret itself may contain \fB=\fR. Repeat for more secrets. Plain secrets passed as arguments are named \fBapiKey1\fR, \fBapiKey2\fR, and so on.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B <input>
The input you wish to obfuscate. Typically, an API key

.SH EXAMPLES
.B obfuscate -h
.br
Show help information.
.TP
.B obfuscate ABCD1234
.br
Produce a Secrets file that will decode the obfuscated data back to ABCD1234
.TP
.B obfuscate --key openAI=sk-abc123 --key stripe=pk_live_xyz
.br
Produce a Secrets file with properties \fBSecrets.openAI\fR and \fBSecrets.stripe\fR

